[
  {
    "uid": "C0483",
    "text": "Small inherited changes can accumulate across many generations. Deep geological time gives that process a scale far beyond a human lifetime.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2784,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-cumulative-evolution",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0484",
    "text": "Selection can reshape life across deep time",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2785,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-cumulative-evolution",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0485",
    "text": "Lamarck and Darwin\u2013Wallace accounts both allow species to change. Lamarck's use, disuse and inherited acquired changes differ from selection acting on inherited variation. Agreement that species change does not erase disagreement about how.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2786,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-changed-meaning-of-kinds",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0486",
    "text": "Changing species, different accounts of how",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2787,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-changed-meaning-of-kinds",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0487",
    "text": "Evolutionary change requires inherited differences to persist across generations. How that happened remained unresolved in these nineteenth-century arguments.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2788,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-open-heredity",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0488",
    "text": "Cumulative evolution with heredity still unresolved",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2789,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-open-heredity",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0489",
    "text": "Powered machinery and specialized tasks increase the scale of production. The factory combines a technology with a way of organizing people.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2790,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-industrial-production",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0490",
    "text": "Specialized labour at machine scale",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2791,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-industrial-production",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0491",
    "text": "Industrial output depends on a continuing fuel supply. Its apparent power has material costs and consequences.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2792,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-fuel-dependent-industry",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0492",
    "text": "Industrial power has a material appetite",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2793,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-fuel-dependent-industry",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0493",
    "text": "In Marx's critique, workers can lose control over their activity and its products. The problem is a relationship of ownership and power, not simply disliking a task.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2794,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-alienated-work",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0494",
    "text": "The maker can lose control of the work",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2795,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-alienated-work",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0495",
    "text": "Morris proposes work that produces useful things while giving the maker worthwhile activity. It is an alternative to assess, not a completed solution to economic organization.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2796,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-useful-pleasurable-work",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0496",
    "text": "Useful work need not erase the maker",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2797,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-useful-pleasurable-work",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0497",
    "text": "Cooperation can help organisms survive and reproduce. Recognizing its importance does not refute natural selection.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2798,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-cooperation-in-evolution",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0498",
    "text": "Mutual aid belongs inside the question of survival",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2799,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-cooperation-in-evolution",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0499",
    "text": "Nature includes cooperation as well as competition. Neither fact by itself tells people how a society ought to be governed.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2800,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-competitive-story-limited",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0500",
    "text": "Nature is not a competition-only morality tale",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2801,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-competitive-story-limited",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0501",
    "text": "A labour-saving machine may still leave workers with less say over their pace and decisions. Reduced effort and greater control are separate gains.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2802,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-control-of-work",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0502",
    "text": "Mechanized effort can deepen lost control",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2803,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-control-of-work",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0503",
    "text": "The microscope reveals living things too small for unaided sight. Discovering them expands knowledge without automatically explaining which ones cause illness.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2804,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-microscopic-life",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0504",
    "text": "A previously unseen living world",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2805,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-microscopic-life",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0505",
    "text": "Cholera deaths differ between comparable households using different water supplies. This supports investigating water as a cause while still checking other differences and the quality of records.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2806,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-waterborne-pattern",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0506",
    "text": "Cholera mortality tracks a water-supply difference",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2807,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-waterborne-pattern",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0507",
    "text": "The cholera comparison points toward contaminated water as a preventable route of disease. Avoiding that water can be justified before everyone agrees about the complete microscopic cause.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2808,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-prevention-before-settlement",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0508",
    "text": "A useful intervention before full agreement",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2809,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-prevention-before-settlement",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0509",
    "text": "One account blames cholera on foul air; another connects it with contaminated water. Comparing the water-supply evidence challenges the rival explanations without pretending they have equal support.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2810,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-competing-disease-accounts",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0510",
    "text": "Foul air or a waterborne cause?",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2811,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-competing-disease-accounts",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0511",
    "text": "Air reaches both broths, but dust reaches only one, and only that broth develops growth. The comparison supports microorganisms arriving with dust rather than air alone producing life.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2812,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-microbial-growth",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0512",
    "text": "Broth growth tracks incoming microorganisms",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2813,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-microbial-growth",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0513",
    "text": "Living cultures participate in changes such as fermentation. Biological activity becomes part of the explanation of material transformation.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2814,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-living-fermentation",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0514",
    "text": "Organisms participate in chemical change",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2815,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-living-fermentation",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0515",
    "text": "Yeast extract ferments even without intact yeast cells. Buchner's later result shows that some of the chemistry can operate outside a whole living cell, revising the earlier claim without erasing microorganisms' role.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2816,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-chemical-agency-in-cells",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0516",
    "text": "Living activity includes separable chemistry",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2817,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-chemical-agency-in-cells",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0517",
    "text": "The compass response shows that electricity can have a magnetic effect. Forces need not work through a visible mechanical push.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2818,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-electromagnetic-link",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0518",
    "text": "Electricity acts magnetically",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2819,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-electromagnetic-link",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0519",
    "text": "Changing a magnetic field can produce a current. The effect provides a way to generate electrical action.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2820,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-induction",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0520",
    "text": "A changing field can produce a current",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2821,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-induction",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0521",
    "text": "A field describes how physical influence varies throughout space. The surroundings become part of the explanation, not just empty distance between objects.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2822,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-field-description",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0522",
    "text": "The surrounding space becomes part of the account",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2823,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-field-description",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0523",
    "text": "The linked electrical and magnetic account predicts waves travelling at light's speed. Light becomes part of the same physical theory.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2824,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-electromagnetic-light",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0524",
    "text": "Light belongs to the electromagnetic field",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2825,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-electromagnetic-light",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0525",
    "text": "A reference time can be sent by electrical signals to distant clocks. People no longer have to rely only on carrying a clock between places.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2826,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-networked-time",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0526",
    "text": "Clock coordination travels over a network",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2827,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-networked-time",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0527",
    "text": "Railway stations adopt a shared time so that timetables agree. That practical standard differs from each place's own solar time.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2828,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-standard-time",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0528",
    "text": "A shared railway time",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2829,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-standard-time",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0529",
    "text": "Light produces a lasting image on a prepared surface. The image records an exposure, but still requires choices about the setup and interpretation.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2830,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-photographic-trace",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0530",
    "text": "Light leaves a lasting image",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2831,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-photographic-trace",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0531",
    "text": "A photograph records the view chosen by the photographer. Its physical connection to the scene does not make everything outside the frame visible.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2832,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-framed-photograph",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0532",
    "text": "A photograph records from a selected viewpoint",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2833,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-framed-photograph",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0533",
    "text": "Many prints can be made from one negative. Wider circulation changes who can see the image without making its framing neutral.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2834,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-reproducible-image",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0534",
    "text": "The image can circulate in many copies",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2835,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-reproducible-image",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0535",
    "text": "William James describes experience as a changing but connected flow. Attention shifts while earlier thoughts continue to shape the next moment.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2836,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-inner-continuity",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0536",
    "text": "Experience has a moving continuity",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2837,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-inner-continuity",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0537",
    "text": "An experience has qualities and continuity that a sequence of clock readings does not describe. This does not make clocks useless or inaccurate.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2838,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-lived-duration",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0538",
    "text": "Lived time is not a row of clock units",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2839,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-lived-duration",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0539",
    "text": "Freud's approach reads a dream for hidden wishes and conflicts. It is an interpretive proposal, not the same kind of result as a physical measurement.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2840,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-interpreted-dream",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0540",
    "text": "A dream can be read for concealed conflict",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2841,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-interpreted-dream",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0541",
    "text": "The writer loosens ordinary planning to follow words and associations. Surrealists use this as an artistic experiment, not a verified diagnosis.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2842,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-automatic-writing",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0542",
    "text": "Writing without the usual planned control",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2843,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-automatic-writing",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0543",
    "text": "An unexpected combination makes familiar things seem strange. The artwork asks the viewer to reconsider ordinary associations and expectations.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2844,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-surreal-encounter",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0544",
    "text": "The familiar becomes strangely connected",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2845,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-surreal-encounter",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0545",
    "text": "An artwork can raise questions about ordinary life and society. It need not merely illustrate an already finished theory.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2846,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-art-beyond-illustration",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0546",
    "text": "An artwork can challenge ordinary life",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2847,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-art-beyond-illustration",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0547",
    "text": "Railway clocks coordinate public events, while descriptions of lived time address memory and experience. These answer different questions; a remembered melody does not refute a working clock.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2848,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-plural-access-to-time",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0548",
    "text": "Measured coordination and lived duration",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2849,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-plural-access-to-time",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0549",
    "text": "The flashes are simultaneous in the platform frame. In the train frame, equal paths and the same light speed mean their different arrival times imply different emission times. The disagreement concerns simultaneity after accounting for travel time, not just a delayed signal.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2850,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-frame-dependent-simultaneity",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0550",
    "text": "Different frames need not agree on distant simultaneity",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2851,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-frame-dependent-simultaneity",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0551",
    "text": "Observers moving steadily relative to one another use the same physical laws but need not agree on distant simultaneity. Newton's mechanics remains a useful approximation in everyday conditions.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2852,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-special-relativity",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0552",
    "text": "No preferred inertial frame or universal distant present",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2853,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-special-relativity",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0553",
    "text": "Newton's theory uses a common absolute time. Relativity shows that distant simultaneity depends on the reference frame, while Newton's treatment remains a useful approximation in familiar conditions.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2854,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-newtonian-limit",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0554",
    "text": "Newton\u2019s shared time is a useful limit, not universal",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2855,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-newtonian-limit",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0555",
    "text": "A person in a freely falling room can locally feel weightless. Einstein uses the relation between gravity and acceleration to motivate a new account; this does not make gravitational differences vanish everywhere.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2856,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-local-equivalence",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0556",
    "text": "Free fall connects gravity and acceleration",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2857,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-local-equivalence",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0557",
    "text": "In Einstein's account, matter and the geometry of space and time affect the paths bodies follow. Gravity is no longer described only as a force acting across fixed space.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2858,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-geometric-gravity",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0558",
    "text": "Gravity changes the geometry of paths",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2859,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-geometric-gravity",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0559",
    "text": "Einstein's gravitational theory predicts a change in the path of light near the Sun. Eclipse observations test that consequence, with measurement uncertainty and interpretation still part of the evidence.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2860,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-tested-light-bending",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0560",
    "text": "A new geometry meets a light observation",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2861,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-tested-light-bending",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0561",
    "text": "Continents can be placed in a proposed earlier arrangement and compared. The reconstruction must fit evidence, not just look like a puzzle.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2862,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-reassembled-continents",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0562",
    "text": "Continents can be compared in an earlier arrangement",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2863,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-reassembled-continents",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0563",
    "text": "Matching fossils and rock formations strengthen the case that separated continents share a past. Several kinds of evidence matter more than an outline resemblance alone.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2864,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-continental-drift-case",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0564",
    "text": "Separated lands share a geological past",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2865,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-continental-drift-case",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0565",
    "text": "The patterns support movement, but the proposed driving forces remain inadequate. Evidence for a history can be stronger than its current explanation of how it happened.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2866,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-drift-without-drive",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0566",
    "text": "A strong pattern, an unresolved driving account",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2867,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-drift-without-drive",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0567",
    "text": "Radioactive decay can turn a mineral into a measure of elapsed time. Interpreting it requires checking whether later events changed the material.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2868,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-mineral-clock",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0568",
    "text": "A rock can contain a measurable clock",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2869,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-mineral-clock",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0569",
    "text": "Rock layers give an order of events, but radioactive decay supplies a measure of elapsed time. Mineral evidence can now address how many years passed, provided its later history is understood.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2870,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-absolute-age-possible",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0570",
    "text": "The sequence can acquire durations",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2871,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-absolute-age-possible",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0571",
    "text": "New ocean floor forms at ridges and moves away on both sides. This process explains the paired magnetic patterns.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2872,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-seafloor-spreading",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0572",
    "text": "Ocean floor is made and moves away from ridges",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2873,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-seafloor-spreading",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0573",
    "text": "Continents move as parts of rigid plates made of crust and the uppermost mantle. Plate tectonics is not simply Wegener's original mechanism declared correct.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2874,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-mobile-plates",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0574",
    "text": "Continents move with plates of rigid outer Earth",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2875,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-mobile-plates",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0575",
    "text": "Plates form, move and descend at different boundaries. These processes fit together without requiring Earth to grow steadily larger.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2876,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-recycled-crust",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0576",
    "text": "Plates form, move and descend",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2877,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-recycled-crust",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0577",
    "text": "Continents move as parts of plates, changing the locations and connections of habitats. Patterns of living things must therefore be explained on a changing surface rather than a fixed map.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2878,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-relocated-habitats",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0578",
    "text": "Life\u2019s changing map includes moving land",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2879,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-relocated-habitats",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0579",
    "text": "Logical relationships can be represented and manipulated with symbols. The form of an argument becomes something that can be worked on systematically.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2880,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-boolean-logic",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0580",
    "text": "Inference becomes a manipulable symbolic system",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2881,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-boolean-logic",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0581",
    "text": "A circuit carries out logical operations through switching. Correct operation does not prove that the information supplied to it is true.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2882,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-logic-circuit",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0582",
    "text": "Logical operations become switching actions",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2883,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-logic-circuit",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0583",
    "text": "A symbol machine follows explicit rules for reading, writing and moving through its work. The procedure can be described separately from the particular machine that carries it out.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2884,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-mechanical-procedure",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0584",
    "text": "A rule-governed symbol machine",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2885,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-mechanical-procedure",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0585",
    "text": "One machine can follow many procedures when their instructions are encoded as data. It is not limited to one permanently built-in task.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2886,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-universal-computation",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0586",
    "text": "One machine can follow many encoded procedures",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2887,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-universal-computation",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0587",
    "text": "No program can always work out whether any other program will eventually stop or run forever. This limits one universal test, not the usefulness of programs in general.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2888,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-computation-limit",
